      <p>This entry is repository work. The 11:07 production snapshot is not this pull request. UvA’s Dutch-taught bachelor page lists NT2-II, CNaVT STRT, CNaVT EDUP, and ITNA B2 as test options, and lists diploma exemptions separately. The Portuguese nationality overview was read; the older guide URL ended on an error page, so it is not a profile selector. Service-Public F11926 supports the B2 nationality wording that was read; the Ministry URL was not re-opened, and one TCF IRN page is not treated as proof that FEI materials contradict each other. The Migri YKI combination page was not re-read, so the pairing list was removed. The Foreign Ministry citizenship URL returned a challenge page. Product pages no longer offer a future availability update. Spain and France category isolation is now an explicit noindex flag. The header source-review date on an edited isolated page stays the earlier check; 2026-11-14 is the edit date. The Italian requirement page does not say unread authority pages list other certificates. The DELE A2 page does not treat the 2026-11-14 Cervantes maintenance notice as nationality acceptance. Advertising runtime stays off.</p>

